    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Bidirectional vertex value iterator.</para><para>Iterates over the vertex values in a list, returning the user-defined value (type <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1ab6aa43dd305f98d4cdcaee4defe11c94" kindref="member">VertexValue</ref>) when dereferenced. <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1Vertex" kindref="compound">Vertex</ref> iterators are stable across insert and erase operations. The difference between <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1VertexValueIterator" kindref="compound">VertexValueIterator</ref> and <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstVertexValueIterator" kindref="compound">ConstVertexValueIterator</ref> is that the latter returns const references when dereferenced. <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref> <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1VertexValueIterator" kindref="compound">VertexValueIterator</ref> can be impliciatly converted to a <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Container_1_1Graph_1_1ConstVertexValueIterator" kindref="compound">ConstVertexValueIterator</ref>. </para>    </detaileddescription>
